{%- set power = (@@JSON_YASNO_POWER@@ | from_json) -%}
{%- set schedule = states(power) -%}
{#- The state is only authoritative while its own slot covers now: between
    polls the integration can still publish an expired or upcoming slot. -#}
{%- set slot_start = as_timestamp(state_attr(power, 'event_start'), none) -%}
{%- set slot_end = as_timestamp(state_attr(power, 'event_end'), none) -%}
{%- set covered = slot_start is not none and slot_end is not none and slot_start <= as_timestamp(now()) < slot_end -%}
{%- set restoration = as_datetime(states((@@JSON_YASNO_NEXT_POWER@@ | from_json)), none) -%}
{%- set remaining = (as_timestamp(restoration) - as_timestamp(now())) if restoration is not none else none -%}
{%- set hours = (remaining / 3600) | round(0) | int if remaining is not none else 0 -%}
{%- set load = states((@@JSON_MULTIPLUS_OUTPUT_POWER_L1@@ | from_json)) -%}
{#- Sentences stay flush-left and each tag trims its own trailing newline, so
    every sentence renders on one line without indentation or blank lines. -#}
City power is off.
{% if schedule == 'outage' and covered -%}
This is a scheduled outage.
{% if remaining is not none and remaining > 0 -%}
{% if remaining < 3600 -%}
Power should be back on in less than an hour.
{% else -%}
Power should be back on in about {{ hours }} {{ 'hour' if hours == 1 else 'hours' }}.
{% endif -%}
{% else -%}
No information about how long the outage will last.
{% endif -%}
{% elif schedule == 'normal' and covered -%}
This is not a scheduled outage.
{% elif schedule in ['outage', 'normal'] -%}
The outage schedule does not cover the current time, so I cannot confirm whether this outage is scheduled.
{% else -%}
The outage schedule is unavailable, so I cannot confirm whether this outage is scheduled.
{% endif -%}
Battery is at {{ states((@@JSON_BATTERY_CHARGE@@ | from_json)) | int('unknown') }} percent.
{% if is_number(load) %}Current power draw is {{ load | float | round(0) | int }} Watts.{% else %}Current power draw is unavailable.{% endif %}